Z||000000||loafer87gt||04-05-2000||01:05 PM||||I know that the factory wheels are 15x7 +35 offset, but I found some great looking wheels at OK tire that are on special for spring. They are 16x8 size though. I know I would have to change the offset,but would this cause steering problems on the front end? THanks.<P>BTW, check them out at <A HREF="http://www.aaatire.com" TARGET=_blank>www.aaatire.com</A>  <P>They are the American Eagle type 77's. With tax, I can get all four of them for $640 Canadian!||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||04-05-2000||01:13 PM||||with a 38 or 40mm offset you'll be ok... running a 245-45 will give you the foot print you need.. and 225-50 up front. What tires are you looking at?  The offset of my 17x8.5 is 42mm.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87PegasusGT||04-05-2000||03:17 PM||||I really want the Mangels Series 77 they show. Is there a way to get an offset that will let them fit?||||reg||1
Z||000003||88 Fiero||04-05-2000||04:52 PM||||First, find out whats the offset of the wheels that your interested in. The wheels that I have in my ride...fronts are 17x7.5 with an offset of 42mm and the rears are 17x8.5 with an offset of 40mm. I have 255/35's in the rears riding in coilovers...and 235/40's in the fronts....||||reg||1
